      "text": "We can use the Pythagorean theorem to solve this problem. The traveler's journey forms a right triangle, with the north-south leg being 18 miles (north) and the east-west leg being 11 miles (west) + 6 miles (east) = 17 miles. The distance from the starting point is the hypotenuse of this right triangle.\n\nUsing the Pythagorean theorem:\n\\[ \\text{distance}^2 = 18^2 + 17^2 \\]\n\\[ \\text{distance}^2 = 324 + 289 \\]\n\\[ \\text{distance}^2 = 613 \\]\n\\[ \\text{distance} = \\sqrt{613} \\]\n\nThe distance from the starting point after the four legs of the journey is \\boxed{\\sqrt{613}} miles.",
